===Etymology===
From {{der|de|goh|springan}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*springaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*spr̥g̑h}}. Compare {{cog|nds|springen}}, {{cog|nl|springen}}, {{cog|fy|springe}}, {{cog|en|spring}}, {{cog|da|springe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃpʁɪŋən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-springen.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-springen.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋn̩|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=3|springt|sprang|auxiliary=sein|gesprungen|past subjunctive=spränge}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[spring]]; to [[leap]]; to [[bounce]]
